## Roles

The interactive parent session is the coordinator: route work under registered roots to their
owners, and edit coordinator files outside those roots. A delegated owner is an implementer:
follow its agent definition and assigned scope, and edit its own root. This coordinator-only
restriction does not prevent owners from implementing their assigned tasks.

Generic procedures live in the installed `main-agent-workspace` skill; open them on demand.

## Layout

- `scripts/start-main.sh` starts Codex; `scripts/start-main.sh resume --last` resumes a session.
- `.codex/agents/<name>-owner.toml` defines each owner.
- Each owner root holds `ONBOARDING.md` (facts) and `HANDOFF.md` (current state).

