|---|---|---|---|---|---|

## Work coordination

- Use Codex subagents for owner tasks; read each owner's TOML instructions if a named role
  is unavailable. Never run two writers for the same root at once.
- Pass the goal, paths, existing decisions, boundaries, acceptance criteria, and report shape.
- Owners read across roots as permitted and edit only their assigned paths. Report cross-owner
  changes to the coordinator, which routes them in dependency order.
- Rebuild context from `ONBOARDING.md` and `HANDOFF.md`; do not assume private agent memory.
- Track long-running jobs by session/job ID, logs, and exit status. An owner can hand monitoring
  to the parent, but the parent continues until requested results are collected or a user
  checkpoint is reached. A launched build is not a completed build.
- Honor user instructions and existing authorization; ask only for missing material decisions.

